From 5899100e5bc4be25d5a3149930dc8ace0acedc09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:59:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 152/152] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-asus-zenbook-a16: drive the
 RGB camera MCLK at 6 mA

The OV02C10 reference clock (MCLK4, GPIO100, 19.2 MHz) is driven at the
2 mA that glymur.dtsi sets for cam_mclk4_default. On this board, enabling
the internal DMIC clock then puts horizontal bands into every frame and
stretches the frame interval from 33.27 ms to about 36 ms: row
high-pass RMS goes from about 1 to 15-20 raw10 units. Windows programs
GPIO100 at 6 mA (CAMP_RES TLMM settings), and at 6 mA the bands and the
frame stretch are gone with the microphone running.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
index 851979224e35..3f69a9d09d0a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
@@ -2368,3 +2368,7 @@ map0 {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+&cam_mclk4_default {
+	drive-strength = <6>;
+};
